.vscode/**
src/**
test/**
out/*.cjs
out/**/*.map
node_modules/**
tsconfig.json
esbuild.mjs
**/*.ts
.gitignore
tools/**

# PACKAGING (docs/CONTRACTS.md §11.25): `core/` is the analyzer the VSIX
# SHIPS, written only by `tools/sync-core.py` and gated by `tools/verify.py --vsix`.
# It must stay in the package - without it a marketplace install on a machine with a
# bare Python has no analyzer at all - so it is negated explicitly rather than left to
# the absence of a pattern, and only its bytecode residue is excluded.
#
# C2: `core/` is now GITIGNORED and built by `npm run compile` / `vscode:prepublish`.
# That makes this negation load-bearing in a second way: vsce falls back to
# `.gitignore` only when this file is absent, so the rule that keeps the bundled
# analyzer in the package lives here and nowhere else. The `packaging` CI job proves
# the result by running the analyzer out of the packaged VSIX
# (`vscode-extension/tools/vsix_smoke.py`), and `tools/sync-core.mjs` is what builds
# the directory in the first place, so it is never merely stale - it is absent, and
# `scripts/vsix_check.py` fails loudly on that.
!core/**
core/**/__pycache__/**
**/*.pyc
**/*.pyo
